# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw data — the lake lives in S3, not in git.
#
# `data/orders.csv` (1.3 GB) and `data/order_items.csv` (955 MB) are both far
# above GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit. Representative 5,000-row extracts
# are committed under `data/samples/` instead; see docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md for
# how to obtain or regenerate the full files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/orders.csv
data/order_items.csv
data/menu.xlsx

# Anything else large that lands in data/ by accident
data/**/*.parquet
data/**/*.avro
data/**/*.zip
data/**/*.gz
data/**/*.7z
!data/samples/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets & credentials — never commit these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.p8
*.key
credentials.json
secrets.yml
profiles.yml
!profiles.example.yml
.aws/
.snowflake/
*_rsa_key*

